# GitHub shows "Cite this repository" from this file, and Zenodo archives each GitHub release with
# a DOI using the same details. doi is the concept DOI: it stands for every version and resolves
# to the newest one.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ZEUS Terminal in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ZEUS Terminal: the self-hosted options trading terminal"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24205410
abstract: >-
  ZEUS Terminal (宙斯期权终端) is a self-hosted options trading terminal that runs on your own
  computer: live positions and Greeks, P/L and risk, paper trading with option and stock legs, a
  stock picker, a news desk, earnings and SEC filings, and a trade journal, with an MCP endpoint
  for AI agents.
authors:
  - name: "ZEUS Terminal contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jackson-cmd/zeus-options-terminal"
url: "https://jackson-cmd.github.io/zeus-options-terminal/"
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
keywords:
  - options trading
  - trading terminal
  - greeks
  - paper trading
  - trade journal
  - self-hosted
  - mcp-server
